{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T03:54:47.662Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"5d97cc75851de74b9275ff63","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-sbqn4h"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"MCP pm_comments lists only the newest 20 comments by default: the backward output cursor stops at that producer page and the last page reports has_more without a continuation"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-11-08 by the CodeRabbit review of PR 1685. A pm_comments MCP listing without limit or full is bounded by the producer to the newest 20 comments (runMcpCommentsAction sets limit 20 and includeMeta), with total_count and has_more true when more exist. A universal output cursor pages only within that producer page. On an item with more than 20 comments, following next_cursor backwards under a small outputBudget therefore stops after the 20th-newest comment. The last page still reports has_more true (from the producer) but carries no next_cursor, so an agent cannot tell how to reach older comments except by restarting with options.limit or options.full true, which the tool description mentions. Expected: when the producer page is exhausted, the envelope names the producer continuation, for example a cursor or a suggested limit for the next older window, so has_more true never arrives without an executable continuation. Duplicate check: searched MCP comments default 20 has_more continuation producer page. pm-gh1679 (open) owns a producer cursor for item history, which is the analogous design, and pm-8s53lj (closed) made the output cursor page backwards within the producer page."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","annotations","continuation","mcp","read-output"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-08T03:54:47.662Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T03:54:47.662Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"An MCP comments listing whose producer page is exhausted names a continuation to the next older window, or reports has_more only when a continuation is present; A spec drives tools/call on more than 20 comments and reaches the oldest comment by following continuations alone"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Through MCP tools/call, list pm_comments on an item with more than 20 comments with a small outputBudget and follow next_cursor until it disappears, then read has_more"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"has_more true always comes with an executable continuation that reaches older comments beyond the producer page"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"After the newest 20 comments the page reports has_more true and no next_cursor; only restarting with options.limit or options.full reaches older comments"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-8s53lj","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-08T03:54:47.662Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1679","kin